is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router6
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Router6’s host firewall (Linux iptables), specifically the FORWARD chain on interface eth2 (10.50.1.2 toward the core).

Mechanism: Location A (172.16.10.0/24) can reach other external sites (e.g., pc4→pc12 192.168.200.12 succeeds), and routing tables across R0–R3–R6 all contain valid RIP routes to 172.18.51.0/24. However, packets destined to Location C (172.18.51.0/24) must transit router6 and are being dropped by firewall rules that block all forwarded traffic arriving on eth2. Direct pings to router6’s own interfaces succeed (e.g., pc4→172.18.50.254), because INPUT policy is ACCEPT; only transit traffic is filtered.

Localization: Router6, interface eth2 (10.50.1.2). Evidence: iptables on rout
